"""Central Barrens hub: story speeches, and names and places the old accept line used to carry."""

STORY = {
    'cb_thunder_and_slumber': ("There are two more, and then the ring can be walked in either direction, which it hasn't been in years. Back in the Wailing Caverns, south-west of the oasis, Lord Pythas holds the east gallery with thunder and sleep, Skum holds the north with thunder alone, and the Deviate Ravagers run the galleries between. They aren't working together, and I've watched parties go in and fight them like a pair and lose for it. Kill one and the ring's still shut, so both have to go. Pythas casts sleep, so carry a trinket or bring someone who can wake you, and Skum's roar weakens your arms, so kill him before it stacks.", 'Keep someone awake at the back. If the whole party sleeps at once, Pythas takes his time.'),
    'cb_sentinel_stingers': ("The Sentinel Rocks are the sandstone teeth north-east of the farm. They're the best shelter on these plains, the only shade a herd can lie down in between here and the hills, and no kodo has slept there in three weeks.\n\nRedstone Scorpids have taken the crevices. I could work round that alone. You move the herd, and you lose a season instead of animals. But something bigger has taken the scorpids. I've been close enough to see how they're behaving, and they aren't holding that ground for themselves. There's a brood-queen in those rocks, and they're hers.\n\nKill the scorpids, and the Redrock Matriarch when she shows her face. She will, once you've made a mess of the nursery.", None),
    'cb_kodo_graveyard': ("East of the Sentinel Rocks, the plain rises into a shallow bowl. The kodo have always walked into it when their time came. Nobody drives them, they just go. I've made that walk with three herds. You go in with them, you stand at the lip, and you come back on your own, and that's the oldest arrangement my people have with those animals.\n\nIt isn't quiet in there any more. The dead don't stay dead. I've watched a cow I knew by name get up again, and I still haven't decided how I feel about that.\n\nWalk in and look round, and put down what the bowl's still holding: the Kodo Wraiths first, then the big horned one the herders call Hollowhorn, if he's still wandering. Kodo aren't meant to come back.", None),
    'cb_cobrahn_and_kresh': ("Two of the warren's masters sit on the western ring, and they aren't the same kind of problem. Lord Cobrahn has begun to prefer his serpent form. That's the Fang's phrase, and what it means is that he's stopped coming back, and at some point he stopped meaning to.\n\nThen there's Kresh, a river-turtle old enough to remember when this pool was a pool. Kresh isn't evil. Kresh is hurt. That won't matter at all in the fight, but it matters to me, and I'd like it said before you go.\n\nCobrahn's in his den to the west, Kresh is in the pool further north, and the Deviate Shamblers hold the ring between them. Kresh pulls into its shell and hits hard coming out, so don't crowd it when it closes. Cobrahn's venom lingers, so bring something that cures it.", None),
    'cb_lady_of_the_fang': ("Lady Anacondra was my student, long ago. I taught her the water, and the way the warren feeds it, and how to tell a sick animal from an angry one, which is the first lesson and the one everything else rests on. She was the first of the Fang to forget which was the lesson and which was the sickness.\n\nShe keeps the Serpentbloom Cavern in the Wailing Caverns now, south-west of the oasis, and her druids hold the river crossing below it. I'd ask you to end it gently. I know it won't go that way, and I'm asking anyway, because I'd rather have asked.\n\nThe Deviate Lashers grip the river's edge, and she waits above them. She'll heal through anything you throw at her unless you move on her fast. She was always better at that than I was.", None),
    'cb_voidcaller_veshra': ("Veshra is their field commander, and she's the reason that circle is going up on schedule. She's a voidcaller, with a smile like a razor and a written list of the things she's summoned.\n\nShe's stationed at the canyon mouth of Dreadmist Peak, north of here, and she isn't casting. She's supervising, walking the circle, correcting people and sending things back to be redone. That's why I want her and not the ritual. The circle is stone and paint, and anybody can lay stone. She's the one who knows whether it's right. If she falls, it falters.\n\nThe Dreadmist Cultists round the circle feed her power, so kill them first, and then her, before anyone there works out the right order to do things in.", None),
}
